  "mach:judgementReason": "Well-structured deep learning framework for accelerated MRI reconstruction from the AI for Oncology group at the Netherlands Cancer Institute. Apache-2.0, 302 stars and 49 forks for a specialised research tool reflects solid community adoption. Implements physics-informed and unrolled network approaches, with fastMRI challenge participation confirming benchmark-level quality. Active development through May 2026 despite last formal release being July 2024. Assess for teams building MRI acceleration pipelines or evaluating deep learning reconstruction against clinical baseline methods.",
